# Content and data

Facts live in TypeScript constants and markdown — not in feature templates.

## Typed data

- Shape lives in `src/app/core/models/profile.models.ts`.
- Values live in `src/app/core/data/*.data.ts` (`profile`, `experience`, `projects`, `skills`, `faq`).
- Site identity / JSON-LD base: `content/site.config.json` **and** `src/app/core/site.config.ts` — keep them aligned.
- Leave `siteUrl` empty unless an absolute public origin is required for sitemap/robots.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — copy only in the template
<p>Himanshu Anand is a senior engineer…</p>

// ✅ GOOD — bind PROFILE / EXPERIENCE / PROJECTS
<p>{{ profile.shortAnswer }}</p>
```

## Articles

- Add `content/articles/<slug>.md` with YAML frontmatter: `title`, `description`, `date`, `tags`, `readingTime`.
- Slug = filename without `.md`. Then run `npm run content` (also runs on `prebuild`).
- Do not edit `articles.generated.ts`.

## Voice

- First person in articles is fine; site chrome and FAQ answers speak about Himanshu in third person for AEO (answer-engine) snippets.
- Keep metrics and employers consistent with `experience.data.ts` and `PROFILE.stats`.
